WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.016 --> 00:00:17.698
didn't have time to focus on where she wanted to go when she zapped away from the gorzogs.

2
00:00:18.498 --> 00:00:21.159
When she landed, she found herself by the well.

3
00:00:21.179 --> 00:00:28.402
"That's the Wormwood tree," she thought, staring at the tree growing behind the wall Zira had erected.

4
00:00:28.422 --> 00:00:32.664
"Even though nobody will call it that for years, I suppose."

5
00:00:33.324 --> 00:00:38.807
For someone like her, who wanted to be a researcher, it was a dream come true to travel

6
00:00:38.887 --> 00:00:40.068
to ancient Magica.

7
00:00:41.068 --> 00:00:46.912
But with a shiver of anxiety, she wondered once again how she and Zann would ever travel back

8
00:00:46.972 --> 00:00:47.892
to their own time.

9
00:00:48.693 --> 00:00:51.034
Perda noticed several gorzogs near the wall.

10
00:00:51.514 --> 00:00:56.797
She almost zapped away again but then saw at least two dozen people hanging around nearby.

11
00:00:56.817 --> 00:00:59.939
"Why aren't the gorzogs attacking anyone?"

12
00:01:00.339 --> 00:01:00.759
she thought.

13
00:01:00.779 --> 00:01:03.236
"Perda! Is that you?"

14
00:01:03.736 --> 00:01:04.997
a familiar voice called.

15
00:01:05.497 --> 00:01:06.297
It was Anso.

16
00:01:06.817 --> 00:01:07.537
He hurried over.

17
00:01:07.557 --> 00:01:09.178
"What are you doing here?"

18
00:01:09.458 --> 00:01:10.218
Perda asked him.

19
00:01:10.238 --> 00:01:15.300
"My father heard that the well's waters have special powers," Anso said.

20
00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:18.800
"He brought my mother to see if it might cure her illness."

21
00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:21.521
"What's holding back the gorzogs?"

22
00:01:21.841 --> 00:01:22.461
Perda asked.

23
00:01:23.222 --> 00:01:24.022
Anso shrugged.

24
00:01:24.682 --> 00:01:25.602
"Nobody knows.

25
00:01:26.322 --> 00:01:28.383
But they've been staying right by the wall.

26
00:01:28.823 --> 00:01:31.724
They growl when anyone goes too close."

27
00:01:32.628 --> 00:01:36.129
"I bet Zira figured out how to control them," Perda said.

28
00:01:36.149 --> 00:01:39.630
"She probably ordered them to guard the well."

29
00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:43.771
As she took a step closer, her foot hit something on the ground.

30
00:01:44.331 --> 00:01:49.072
It was a cracked pottery cup—the same one Zira had dropped days earlier.

31
00:01:50.593 --> 00:01:52.673
Perda wondered why it looked so familiar.

32
00:01:53.474 --> 00:02:00.535
Then she gasped as she realized it looked exactly like that ancient, cracked cup at Zann's parents' lab!

33
00:02:01.336 --> 00:02:03.176
"It's a relic," she whispered.

34
00:02:03.196 --> 00:02:06.077
"At least, it will be one someday."

35
00:02:06.097 --> 00:02:07.818
"Where's Mellis?"

36
00:02:08.258 --> 00:02:08.939
Anso asked.

37
00:02:08.959 --> 00:02:10.399
"Is she safe?"

38
00:02:10.419 --> 00:02:13.540
"I'm not sure," Perda said.

39
00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:15.941
"Zann and I are going to help her though.

40
00:02:16.502 --> 00:02:17.922
I just need to find him.

41
00:02:18.763 --> 00:02:20.943
But first, let's heal your mother."

42
00:02:22.784 --> 00:02:24.585
Anso brought Perda to his parents.

43
00:02:25.265 --> 00:02:30.207
At first his mother looked nervous, but she agreed to let Perda try to heal her illness.

44
00:02:30.947 --> 00:02:32.108
Perda was nervous too.

45
00:02:32.696 --> 00:02:36.879
She was good at healing cuts and scrapes, but she'd never healed anything serious.

46
00:02:37.419 --> 00:02:40.541
She created friction and then touched the woman on the arm.

47
00:02:40.561 --> 00:02:43.122
"Heal," she murmured.

48
00:02:43.943 --> 00:02:45.964
Anso's mother immediately looked healthier.

49
00:02:46.504 --> 00:02:48.005
Anso and his father gasped.

50
00:02:48.025 --> 00:02:49.486
"It worked!"

51
00:02:49.886 --> 00:02:50.547
Anso cried.

52
00:02:50.567 --> 00:02:52.348
"Thank you so much!"

53
00:02:52.368 --> 00:02:54.709
"You're welcome," Perda said.

54
00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:59.052
At that moment Zira zapped into view, surrounded by goons.

55
00:02:59.604 --> 00:03:02.845
Krub was there, too, holding onto Zann, who wasn't moving.

56
00:03:02.865 --> 00:03:04.905
"Oh no," Perda thought.

57
00:03:04.925 --> 00:03:08.927
"It looks like Zira did an Immobilization spell on him!"

58
00:03:09.607 --> 00:03:13.868
In her own time, people were supposed to use that spell only in self-defense.

59
00:03:15.208 --> 00:03:19.909
She hid behind a flowering shrub so Zira wouldn't see her while she decided what to do.

60
00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:22.790
Anso came with her, looking confused.

61
00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:27.231
Then Vilkor zapped into view, gripping Mellis' arm.

62
00:03:27.251 --> 00:03:29.192
"Zira!" he cried.

63
00:03:29.676 --> 00:03:32.899
"Please reconsider your decision, my old friend!"

64
00:03:32.919 --> 00:03:34.380
"What decision?"

65
00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:35.481
Anso whispered.

66
00:03:36.022 --> 00:03:37.823
"I don't know," Perda whispered back.

67
00:03:37.843 --> 00:03:41.146
"But we have to get Zann and Mellis away from Zira."

68
00:03:41.786 --> 00:03:44.309
She noticed that neither of her friends was saying anything.

69
00:03:44.969 --> 00:03:48.072
She guessed that Zira had put a Muting spell on both of them.

70
00:03:49.613 --> 00:03:51.835
Vilkor dragged Mellis closer to the others.

71
00:03:51.855 --> 00:03:54.337
"We make such a good team, Zira!"

72
00:03:54.717 --> 00:03:55.358
he exclaimed.

73
00:03:55.378 --> 00:03:57.079
"And you can trust me.

74
00:03:58.036 --> 00:04:00.598
I'll prove my loyalty however you like."

75
00:04:01.499 --> 00:04:05.702
"Really?" Zira smirked, clearly enjoying his groveling.

76
00:04:05.722 --> 00:04:09.486
"Then perhaps I'll give you one more chance.

77
00:04:10.206 --> 00:04:15.911
You can prove your loyalty by tossing your niece to my gorzog guards."

78
00:04:16.811 --> 00:04:19.253
She glanced toward the beasts guarding the wall.

79
00:04:19.274 --> 00:04:21.515
"They're getting hungry."

80
00:04:22.997 --> 00:04:23.917
Vilkor gasped.

81
00:04:25.499 --> 00:04:26.179
So did Perda.

82
00:04:27.564 --> 00:04:30.665
"He won't do it," Anso said, sounding uncertain.

83
00:04:30.685 --> 00:04:31.765
"Will he?"

84
00:04:31.785 --> 00:04:33.686
"Please, Zira!"

85
00:04:34.446 --> 00:04:36.807
Vilkor grabbed her sleeve, looking distraught.

86
00:04:36.827 --> 00:04:39.287
"Choose another test, I beg you.

87
00:04:39.807 --> 00:04:43.188
Mellis is my only family, and she's a good girl.

88
00:04:43.809 --> 00:04:44.929
Well, mostly, anyway!"

89
00:04:44.949 --> 00:04:47.130
"I've made my decision."

90
00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:52.591
Zira shot a cold look at Mellis and then returned her gaze to Vilkor.

91
00:04:52.611 --> 00:04:55.432
"Now you must make yours."

92
00:04:56.876 --> 00:04:57.917
Perda held her breath.

93
00:04:58.517 --> 00:05:03.400
Would Vilkor actually sacrifice Mellis just to get back into Zira's good graces?

94
00:05:04.241 --> 00:05:08.144
She was shocked when Vilkor started shoving Mellis toward the gorzogs.

95
00:05:08.864 --> 00:05:10.605
"Sorry, Mellis," he said.

96
00:05:10.625 --> 00:05:13.067
"This is your own fault, you know.

97
00:05:13.627 --> 00:05:16.009
You should have stuck to our plan."

98
00:05:16.929 --> 00:05:18.791
Then he glanced back at Zira.

99
00:05:18.811 --> 00:05:20.912
"They won't eat me, will they?"

100
00:05:21.272 --> 00:05:22.493
he asked nervously.

101
00:05:22.513 --> 00:05:24.875
"We have to do something!"

102
00:05:25.295 --> 00:05:26.556
Anso whispered urgently.

103
00:05:27.072 --> 00:05:27.732
Perda nodded.

104
00:05:27.752 --> 00:05:29.053
"Leave it to me."

105
00:05:30.554 --> 00:05:32.855
She rubbed her hands together and stepped forward.

106
00:05:33.696 --> 00:05:36.918
Vilkor was still pushing Mellis in the direction of the gorzogs.

107
00:05:37.578 --> 00:05:41.480
The creatures watched, sticky saliva dripping from their snouts.

108
00:05:42.061 --> 00:05:44.042
The largest took a step toward Mellis.

109
00:05:44.682 --> 00:05:46.703
Perda knew she had to act now.

110
00:05:46.723 --> 00:05:52.727
"Blast!" she shouted, sending a strong bolt of magic energy straight at Vilkor.

111
00:05:53.247 --> 00:05:58.294
She felt a touch of guilt, since Blast spells were supposed to be used only in self-defense.

112
00:05:58.874 --> 00:06:02.496
The magic energy hit Vilkor and sent him flying through the air.

113
00:06:03.517 --> 00:06:06.219
But the gorzogs were still creeping toward Mellis.

114
00:06:06.799 --> 00:06:08.680
She backed away, looking anxious.

115
00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:12.722
Perda created friction, preparing to repel the creatures.

116
00:06:13.342 --> 00:06:16.824
At that moment Zing flew into view, panting with exertion.

117
00:06:17.325 --> 00:06:22.608
Perda guessed that Zira and the others had left him behind in the village when they'd zapped out

118
00:06:22.688 --> 00:06:27.866
here. The little dragon must have been flying as fast as he could to reach Zann.

119
00:06:28.567 --> 00:06:33.109
He shot a burst of flame at Zira, who jumped away from Zann to avoid being burned.

120
00:06:33.129 --> 00:06:35.991
"Zing!" Perda shouted.

121
00:06:36.011 --> 00:06:37.391
"Help Mellis!"

122
00:06:39.413 --> 00:06:43.155
Zing spun toward the gorzogs, shooting more fire.

123
00:06:43.215 --> 00:06:48.017
They growled and spit at him, but he had learned their tricks and stayed just out of range.

124
00:06:48.858 --> 00:06:51.039
Meanwhile Zira glared at Perda.

125
00:06:51.059 --> 00:06:53.200
"You!" she hissed.

126
00:06:53.769 --> 00:06:56.400
"You'll regret crossing me, little girl!"
